=== the law and its equation, a row per term at one column, the two sides last as an equality's
    associative: op (op a b) c = op a (op b c)
    a              1
    b              2
    c              3
    op a b         -1
    op b c         -1
    op (op a b) c  -4
    op a (op b c)  2

=== a clause in parentheses; a clause over booleans ends on the fact that breaks it
    order (agrees with equal): cmp a b = 0 iff a = b
    a        1
    b        11
    cmp a b  0
    a = b    false

=== the column is two past the longest name, a side's included
    distributive: op a (over b c) = over (op a b) (op a c)
    a                       1
    b                       2
    c                       3
    over b c                6
    op a b                  3
    op a c                  4
    op a (over b c)         7
    over (op a b) (op a c)  12

=== two single-line sides are marked under their names
    round trip: g (f x) = x
    f x      "the quick brown fox"
    g (f x)  "the quick br0wn f0x"
                          ~    ~
    x        "the quick brown fox"
                          ~    ~

=== on a terminal, colour marks the changed spans and no ~ line prints
    round trip: g (f x) = x
    «d|f x»      "the quick brown fox"
    «d|g (f x)»  "the quick br«G|0»wn f«G|0»x"
    «d|x»        "the quick br«R|o»wn f«R|o»x"

=== under colour off a terminal, the ~ lines print too
    round trip: g (f x) = x
    «d|f x»      "the quick brown fox"
    «d|g (f x)»  "the quick br«G|0»wn f«G|0»x"
                          «G|~    ~»
    «d|x»        "the quick br«R|o»wn f«R|o»x"
                          «R|~    ~»

=== a multi-line term prints under its name, multi-line sides diff under theirs
    commutative: op a b = op b a
    a:
      a
      b
    b       c
    --- op a b
    +++ op b a
    @@ -1,3 +1,3 @@
    + c
      a
      b
    - c

=== two sides a printer shows alike print once
    commutative: op a b = op b a
    a       <v>
    b       <v>
    both sides render as: <v>
    the printer shows less than the equality compares

=== two sides cut to the same kept bytes say what they agree on
    idempotent: f x = x
    the sides agree on the 65536 bytes a failure keeps of each (f x 65537 bytes, x 65537 bytes)

=== two sides that differ by a final newline name the side that has it
    idempotent: f x = x
    values differ only by a trailing newline (on the x side)

=== a term over 800 bytes is elided
    idempotent: f (f x) = f x
    x        … (100 bytes elided)
    f (f x)  1
    f x      2

=== a failed term at a location: failed at, then its entry nested, its name outside the column
    round trip: g (f x) = x
    x    0.0.0-a.1
    f x  "0.0.0-a.1"
    g (f x) failed at:
      test/test_version.ml:32
      expected  Some _
      actual    None

=== a failed term without one: failed with
    equivalence (respelled): a = r a
    a  1.2
    r a failed with:
      uncaught exception:
        Failure("boom")
      Raised at Version.pad in file "lib/version.ml", line 3

=== a ?msg prints above the law
    zero is neutral
    neutral: op e x = x
    e       0
    op e x  -5
    x       5

=== a law's failure is a property's inner failure
    counterexample (case 2, shrunk 6 steps): (1, 2, 3)
    which failed with:
      associative: op (op a b) c = op a (op b c)
      a              1
      b              2
      c              3
      op a b         -1
      op b c         -1
      op (op a b) c  -4
      op a (op b c)  2
    replay: WINDTRAP_SEED=s1:7be1d2c904aa31f5 dune runtest

=== and a failed term nests inside it
    counterexample (case 0): 0.0.0-a.1
    which failed with:
      round trip: g (f x) = x
      x    0.0.0-a.1
      f x  "0.0.0-a.1"
      g (f x) failed at:
        test/test_version.ml:32
        expected  Some _
        actual    None
    replay: WINDTRAP_SEED=s1:7be1d2c904aa31f5 dune runtest

=== under colour the names are faint
    associative: op (op a b) c = op a (op b c)
    «d|a»              1
    «d|b»              2
    «d|c»              3
    «d|op a b»         -1
    «d|op b c»         -1
    «d|op (op a b) c»  «g|-4»
    «d|op a (op b c)»  «r|2»
